// tests/ctl_air_tests.nv — the Link Layer's radio program (`ll_air.nv`)
// on a scripted air: the second implementation of `Radio` and `Timebase`
// (`orbit/noble-radio/src/ll_radio.nv`), beside `Nrf54Air` of `orbit/bsp/nordic/nrf54/blocks/radio_nrf54.nv`.
//
// `SimAir` is a radio with no registers.  Time passes only when the program
// waits (`wait_address`, `wait_phyend`, `wait_rx`, `wait_until`) or when the test
// driver steps it.  The radio follows the contract of the trait:
//
//   start_tx     the first bit is `tx_lead_us` later, the access address 40
//                microseconds after it, and the octets of the packet buffer
//                that `packet` named are latched when the access address comes
//   start_rx     the receiver listens from the ramp-up; a scripted packet whose
//                access address comes while it listens is copied into the
//                buffer that `packet` named
//   arm          at the end of a packet the radio rests, or, T_IFS after the
//                end, starts the transmitter (the packet buffer is read when it
//                starts) or listens; `halt` takes an armed transmitter back
//
// and the peers are a script: the packets they send at given times (`hear`), and
// the packet a peer sends T_IFS after a packet of the Controller's (`react`).
// What the Controller sent is logged with the time of its first bit.
//
// The program runs here as it runs on the DK: `ll_poll` decides which activity
// has the radio and carries it out, and the tests read what went on air, the
// statistics the program keeps and what the Host was told.

